# Copy to .env and edit:  cp .env.example .env
#
# Compose reads this file twice: for the ${...} in docker-compose.yml, and as the
# environment of the relay container. The keys the backend understands are the ones
# in backend/src/relay/shared/config.py; RELAY_BIND, RELAY_PORT and OLLAMA_MODEL are
# Compose's own and the backend ignores them.

# ── The one line that matters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRET_KEY signs every access token. The backend ships a published development
# default and refuses to start while it is still set, unless somebody has said so
# out loud. That is the next line: it is what keeps `docker compose up` a
# two-command demo on your own machine, and it is the first thing to delete before
# anyone else connects.
#   echo "SECRET_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)" >> .env
# SECRET_KEY=
ALLOW_INSECURE_SECRET_KEY=1

# ── Where the node is published ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RELAY_BIND is the host address to answer on: 127.0.0.1 for this machine only,
# 0.0.0.0 for the network. RELAY_PORT is the host port.
RELAY_BIND=127.0.0.1
RELAY_PORT=8000

# ── Database ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both lines are already the right answer for their setup, so neither is set here.
# Unset, the image default is the SQLite file inside the relay-data volume.
# The Postgres URL belongs with docker-compose.override.yml.example, which starts
# the database and sets this to match.
# DATABASE_URL=sqlite+aiosqlite:////data/relay.db
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://relay:relay@postgres:5432/relay
# With docker-compose.override.yml.example copied in, Postgres needs a password:
#   echo "POSTGRES_PASSWORD=$(openssl rand -hex 16)" >> .env
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# ── First account ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# An empty node is otherwise invite-only with no way in. Set both or neither: if
# either is missing, nothing is created and the database is left as it is.
# ADMIN_USERNAME=
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ── Everything else already defaults sensibly ──────────────────────────────────
# VERSION=dev
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO                                  # CRITICAL, ERROR, WARNING, INFO, DEBUG
# WEB_DIST_DIR=/app/web                           # empty disables the web app entirely
# STREAM_KEEPALIVE_SECONDS=30                     # shorten it if a proxy in front drops idle streams

# ── Only for `docker compose --profile ai up` ──────────────────────────────────
# The model the moderation sidecar pulls on first start. RELY-102 has not chosen
# one, so nothing here chooses for you: name anything Ollama can pull and it lands
# in the ollama-models volume. Unset leaves the sidecar running with no model, and
# relay does not notice either way.
# OLLAMA_MODEL=
